Practical Case Study: Traffic Analysis
--------------------------------------
A smart traffic monitoring system is installed across a city to track vehicle speeds using highway
cameras and speed sensors. Every few minutes, the system receives vehicle speeds in random
order from different checkpoints.
Traffic police officials want to analyze the data quickly to identify the slowest and fastest
vehicles on the road. Before generating reports, the system must arrange all vehicle speeds in
ascending order.
Your task is to sort the vehicle speeds using the Bubble Sort algorithm.
During each pass, compare adjacent speeds and swap them if they are in the wrong order.
Continue the process until all speeds are arranged correctly.

Input Format
------------
The first line contains an integer n, representing
the number of vehicles recorded.
The second line contains n space-separated
integers representing vehicle speeds.

Constraints
-----------
1 <= n <= 100
1 <= speed <= 300

Sample Input
------------
5
72 55 90 63 48

Sample Output
-------------
48 55 63 72 90

